# Template: Standard Hallucination Analysis

## File Purpose
This template provides a framework for addressing standard hallucinations that may occur during normal operation. It helps structure the requirements for preventing and handling common types of hallucinations that aren't specifically tied to past chat interactions.

## Usage
```
create-template: rules-workflow @[feature-folder] project-rule-parameter
```

Example:
```
create-template: rules-workflow @69-file-handling project-rule-parameter
```

## Requirements Template

When this template is applied, it will create the following structure in requirements.md:

```markdown
# Standard Hallucination Analysis Requirements

## Hallucination Type
[Describe the category or type of hallucination to be addressed (e.g., file paths, command interpretation, context retention)]

## Trigger Conditions
[What conditions or scenarios typically trigger this type of hallucination?]

## Current Behavior
[How does the system currently behave when this type of hallucination occurs?]

## Desired Behavior
[How should the system behave to prevent or handle this type of hallucination?]

## Detection Mechanisms
[What mechanisms can be implemented to detect this type of hallucination?]

## Prevention Strategy
[What strategies should be implemented to prevent this type of hallucination?]

## Recovery Approach
[If the hallucination occurs, how should the system recover or correct itself?]

## Success Criteria
[What specific criteria will indicate successful prevention/handling of this hallucination type?]

## Implementation Scope
[Which system components need to be modified to implement these improvements?]

## Constraints
[What system behaviors must be preserved while implementing these changes?]
```

## Template Application

When the create-template command is received, I will:
1. Create or update requirements.md with this template
2. Leave all sections empty for Tyler to fill in
3. Wait for Tyler to complete the requirements before proceeding with any planning

